PC0, PC1, PC2 — Desktop > IP Configuration > DHCP.
Expected addresses are in 192.168.10.10–192.168.10.50.
Command Prompt:
ipconfig /all
ping 192.168.10.1
ping 192.168.10.2

Reconnect test:
1. Set PC0 to DHCP.
2. Disconnect and reconnect its switch cable (or disable/enable the interface).
3. Click DHCP again if needed; verify with `ipconfig`.
4. Ping 192.168.10.1 and 192.168.10.2.

Router checks:
show ip interface brief
show ip dhcp binding
show ip dhcp pool
show ip nat translations
show ip nat statistics

Packet Tracer Simulation:
1. Switch to Simulation mode.
2. Filter for DHCP and ARP; use PC Desktop > IP Configuration > DHCP.
3. Observe Discover, Offer, Request, ACK (DORA).
4. For NAT, generate traffic from a PC to a simulated outside server; inspect the packet and `show ip nat translations`.
